  "slides": [
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "eyebrow": "01 · The thesis",
      "title": "The technology is not the story. The cost line is.",
      "body": "Health care is a data-rich, decision-poor industry. The binding constraints are trial cost, regulatory evidence and reimbursement, not ideas. AI and automation shorten the path from target to patient, but only companies that generate defensible clinical evidence convert that speed into margin."
    },
    {
      "kind": "points",
      "eyebrow": "02 · Sector economics",
      "title": "What this sector actually sells",
      "body": "Value accrues at different points: pharma earns on protected pricing and patent life, medtech on installed base and procedures, providers on volume and payer mix, payers on medical loss ratio.",
      "bullets": [
        "Pharma gross margins are high, but R&D intensity and patent cliffs set the cycle.",
        "Medtech earns on procedure volume and consumables attached to capital equipment.",
        "Providers run thin margins, sensitive to labour cost and payer mix.",
        "Payers earn on the spread between premiums and medical spend.",
        "Reimbursement decisions, not technical feasibility, determine commercial timing."
      ]
    },
    {
